      "ownershipVehicle": "ArcLight Infrastructure Partners Fund VIII",
      "description": "Thunderbird Renewables is an ArcLight Infrastructure Partners Fund VIII portfolio of operating U.S. wind-generation assets managed through ArcLight's SkyVest Renewables platform. Regulatory filings show Fund VIII vehicles acquired a 50% indirect interest in the Lakefield Wind Project on February 21, 2025 and a 100% indirect interest in the Shiloh IV Wind Project on March 12, 2025, then acquired the remaining 50% Lakefield interest on July 1, 2025. ArcLight's 2025 ESG report presents Thunderbird as a 309 MW operating renewables portfolio. Thunderbird is counted as the manager-level portfolio, while SkyVest is the management platform and Lakefield and Shiloh IV are underlying assets. ArcLight's live investments page lists Thunderbird as Current. Public sources reviewed do not disclose Thunderbird's legal suffix, separate website, founding year, headquarters or manager-level ownership percentage, and no Thunderbird-level exit or signed pending transaction was identified through August 15, 2026.",
